Make the local end of line the platform's.

TConfiguration::GetLocalEOLType always says CRLF: core has only run on
Windows, where local text files end their lines so. Text-mode transfers
convert to and from it (SFTP, SCP), so on POSIX a text-mode download gave
local files CRLF line endings, which POSIX programs do not expect, and the
internal editor would have written them back so. The platform's delimiter
tells the two apart in one expression both compilers take: a backslash on
Windows, so upstream's behaviour is unchanged. Line counts are unchanged.

Offered upstream as winscp/winscp#82, where it is an #ifdef _WIN32 at the
maintainer's request: the same choice made at compile time, carried here
as one line to keep the line count; dropped when a pin move brings it in.

--- a/source/core/Configuration.cpp
+++ b/source/core/Configuration.cpp
@@ -2050,1 +2050,1 @@
-  return eolCRLF;
+  return (PathDelim == L'\\') ? eolCRLF : eolLF;
